    {
      "id": "claim_514d45436a954c90995dcde46d6e6f87",
      "statement": "CacheManager offers three constructor shapes — CacheManager(Path), CacheManager(Path, EnvironmentProvider), and CacheManager(Path, CacheReplacementStrategy, List<CacheType>, EnvironmentProvider) — which funnel into the explicit constructor; the no-environment variants fall back to a new SystemEnvironment(), the explicit constructor creates a missing cache directory, throws IllegalArgumentException when the path exists but is not a directory or when the hierarchy list is empty, and null-checks strategy, hierarchy, and environment.",
      "evidence": [
