    {
      "id": "claim_cce6866488a943efb69b050db81c0de8",
      "statement": "buildCacheHierarchy creates one backend per configured CacheType via Cache.createByType, handing every layer the same cache-file path (<cacheDir>/<name>.json, ignored by Redis-based layers) and one ObjectMapper created per hierarchy build, then folds the caches left with the configured CacheReplacementStrategy so the first hierarchy entry becomes the primary of the outermost composite; a single-type hierarchy returns the backend directly without layering.",
